{"resourceIdentifier":"1408","resourceName":"Chyulu Hills REDD+ Project","description":"The Chyulu Hills REDD+ Project (CHRP) is a multi-partner initiative designed to promote climate change mitigation and adaptation, restore biodiversity and create alternative livelihoods under the UN scheme of Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and forest Degradation (REDD+). It is located in the Tsavo-Amboseli ecosystem, southeastern Kenya and stretches over an area of 410,533.84 ha. Its main geographic feature is the volcanic Chyulu Hills mountain range, from which the project derives its name. This project presents a broad ecosystem approach, including REDD+, to provide long-term sustainable financing and management to maintain the ecological integrity of an iconic African landscape. The project will help to protect a very high value wildlife and biodiversity area while supporting the development needs of indigenous and other local communities.","location":{"latitude":-2.806913,"longitude":37.687992},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-08-04","endExclusive":"2021-09-04","endInclusive":"2021-09-03"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1408"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Makueni, Taita Taveta, and Kajiado Counties"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Chyulu Hills Conservation Trust"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1408"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1408"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1100943"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":662473}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCA